\begin{abstract}
    \noindent \textit{The Narrative Consistency Classification System addresses the fundamental challenge of verifying logical coherence across massive, multi-modal textual datasets such as full-length novels. Traditional architectures, primarily the Transformer family, suffer from a "context wall" due to their $O(T^2)$ computational complexity and static context windows. Our system mitigates these constraints via the \textbf{Baby Dragon Hatchling (BDH)} model, a State-Space Model (SSM) optimized for $O(T)$ efficiency and constant memory scaling. By implementing a partitioned \textbf{Entity-Centric World State}, we effectively isolate character-specific causality from global background noise. Consistency is adjudicated via an energy-based \textbf{Counterfactual Consistency Checker}, which mathematically quantifies "surprise" as state perturbation between primary statements and their negations.}
\end{abstract}

\vspace{0.3cm}
